From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] posix: resolver: allow a comment after the nameserver

The resolver gives inet_pton() the rest of the line after "nameserver ".
The udhcpc script of BusyBox writes "nameserver 192.168.1.1 # wlan0",
so inet_pton() fails, no upstream DNS server is found, and the DNS
queries of the Thread devices get no answer.  Take the first word after
"nameserver" as the address, as the C library does.

Upstream: not sent
---
--- a/src/posix/platform/resolver.cpp
+++ b/src/posix/platform/resolver.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <fstream>
+#include <sstream>
 #include <string>
 
 #if OPENTHREAD_CONFIG_DNS_UPSTREAM_QUERY_ENABLE
@@ -119,13 +120,19 @@
 
     while (fp.good() && std::getline(fp, line) && mUpstreamDnsServerCount < kMaxUpstreamServerCount)
     {
-        const char *addressString = &line.c_str()[sizeof(kNameserverItem)];
+        std::istringstream words(line);
+        std::string        item;
+        std::string        address;
+        const char        *addressString;
 
-        // Skip the lines that don't start with "nameserver"
-        if (line.find(kNameserverItem, 0))
+        // Skip the lines that don't start with "nameserver".  The address is the next word: a comment
+        // can follow it, as "# wlan0" in the resolv.conf of the BusyBox udhcpc script.
+        words >> item >> address;
+        if (item != kNameserverItem)
         {
             continue;
         }
+        addressString = address.c_str();
 
         if (inet_pton(AF_INET, addressString, &ip4Address) == 1)
         {
